# Named arguments convention

## Rule

When a function or method has **3 or more parameters**, all call sites must use **named arguments**.

## Also applies when editing

If you edit a function and its parameter count increases from fewer than 3 to 3 or more, update all existing call sites to use named arguments at the same time.

## Examples

```php
// 2 params — positional is fine
$signer->sign($method, $url);

// 3 or more params — named arguments required
$signer->sign(
    method:    $method,
    url:       $url,
    timestamp: time(),
    nonce:     bin2hex(random_bytes(16)),
);
```
